  "title": "Causal World Models in LLM Agents: Bridging Modular Systems and Intervention-Planning",
  "summary": "Causal world models help modular LLM agents by providing intervention-response evidence for cross-module interfaces, improving performance in structured tool environments. These models can beat non-causal lower bounds when intervention-response coverage and local mechanism errors are controlled, and they help in diagnosing agent settings by identifying when causal interfaces are both statistically identifiable and presented in a form the agent can use at action time.",
